    "pmid": "15501593",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1: 14 healthy girls aged 8-10 (children, not adults). I2: during fMRI, participants reappraised sad film clips by distancing, compared with reacting normally. I3 not demonstrated: the analysis used a priori prefrontal ROIs with small-volume correction. The paper says a whole-brain search was also done, but no whole-brain results are reported separately. The Talairach table (Emotion x Regulation interaction) lists corrected P values for prefrontal regions that match the a priori ROIs. Whole-brain coordinates were not demonstrated, so I3 is not met. E2 is likely but unclear."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "19555702",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3",
     "E4"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Healthy adults performed an instructed regulate-vs-view task on emotional pictures during fMRI, so I1 and I2 are met. The authors say they ran whole-brain analyses, but the only reported coordinates (Table 1) are peaks from the between-sex ANOVA. Post hoc tests within each sex were run only at those peaks. No within-group whole-brain coordinate map is reported, so E4 is met and I3 is not demonstrated. A priori regions also used a lenient uncorrected threshold."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21712804",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1 met: 17 healthy women. I2 not met: the task is reappraisal of food desire (craving), not regulation of an emotional response to emotional stimuli. The comparison is REGULATE versus ADMIT desire, not an emotion regulation versus look/passive-viewing comparison. I3 is marked met only loosely: the text gives MNI peaks for ADMIT_TASTY>ADMIT_NONTASTY at uncorrected p<0.001. The regulation coordinates (Table 1) appear only as a figure and are not in the supplied text. Exclusion rests on I2."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "21907809",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "excluded_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1 met: BPD patients, trauma-exposed controls and healthy controls. I2 met: during fMRI, participants were told to increase (UP) or decrease (DOWN, distancing) their emotions, or to maintain them. Maintain is the passive condition. I3 not demonstrated: the within-group whole-brain one-sample t-test results appear only in supplementary Table S3, which was not supplied. The only coordinate table in the text (Table 2) gives between-group differences from the FWE-corrected ROI approach. So no whole-brain within-group stereotaxic coordinates are shown in the available text, and I3 is not_met."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "22613776",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "The participants were remitted MDD patients and healthy controls (I1 met). They down-regulated their emotion by reappraisal or distraction, compared with a view condition, during fMRI (I2 met). However, every analysis was restricted to anatomically defined regions of interest (E2 met). The text contains no coordinate tables; the full list of activations is in a supplement that was not supplied. Whole-brain stereotaxic coordinates were therefore not demonstrated (I3 not met)."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "23712090",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1 and I2 are met: cocaine users with and without Cluster B personality disorders, plus healthy controls, did an fMRI reappraisal task with Observe, Maintain and Suppress (reappraise) instructions. I3 is not demonstrated. The main text gives no stereotaxic peak coordinates for any task contrast, only the PPI seed locations. The authors say the one-sample task activations and whole-brain group comparisons are in Supplementary Tables S1\u2013S7, which were not supplied. The main text reports only between-group findings, which focus on ROIs, so E4 and E2 are unclear. Coordinates may exist in the supplement, so retrieving it could change this decision."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "24760016",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "51 healthy adults viewed, reappraised or suppressed their response to negative pictures, with an attend (look) condition, during fMRI (I1, I2 met). The whole-brain coordinates for the main-effect contrasts (Reappraise vs Attend, Suppress vs Attend, View Negative vs Neutral) are only in Supplementary Table S1, which was not supplied. The only coordinate table in the main text (Table 3) gives whole-brain correlations with alexithymia scores during viewing, not the condition contrasts. The only other coordinate in the text is an amygdala small-volume-correction peak. So the paper does not show whole-brain peak coordinates for a regulation or viewing contrast, and I3 is recorded as not_met."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "25439326",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "I1 met: 56 healthy participants aged 10-22. I2 met: during fMRI, participants used instructed distancing ('far') versus immersed ('close') viewing of aversive pictures, and distancing is a qualifying reappraisal tactic. I3 not demonstrated: the paper says the whole-brain regulation contrasts are in Supplementary Tables 3 and 5, which are not in the supplied text. The main-text tables give only PPI connectivity results (Table 1) and correlations with amygdala decrease (Table 2), and the text gives amygdala ROI peaks only. Re-screen if the supplementary tables become available."
   },
   {
    "pmid": "25617820",
    "decision": "exclude",
    "failed": [
     "I3",
     "E2"
    ],
    "autonima": "included_fulltext",
    "reason": "Adults with remitted MDD and controls (I1) were told to accept, reappraise or simply view sad images during fMRI (I2 met). However, analyses used an a priori small-volume-correction mask covering the frontal lobes and amygdala, and the text says the threshold applied to all analyses. Every reported cluster is frontal or insular. Whole-brain coordinates were not demonstrated (I3 not met), and results are limited to the small-volume mask (E2 met). The reappraise > view results were published earlier and are not reported here."
   },
